 as a formidable warrior and a respected leader. He skillfully employed both defensive and offensive strategies adapting to the evolving military landscape. He was known for his personal courage and leadership inspiring his troops to victory.  He also engaged in diplomatic efforts seeking alliances and maintaining a balance of power.\n\n*Legacy and Death*  Raymond III's reign concluded in 1185 after a period of internal strife and external pressures.  He died in battle during a conflict with the Seljuk Turks.  His death marked the end of an era in Tripoli’s history. He is remembered as a successful ruler who defended the county’s independence and fostered its economic growth.  His reign established Tripoli as a significant power in the Levant and left a lasting impact on its political and economic development. He is considered a pivotal figure in the history of the Crusader states and a symbol of resilience in the face of adversity.  His legacy continues to be studied by historians seeking to understand the complexities of medieval Mediterranean politics and warfare.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.14342188835144043}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.5060096454108134e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0798519179224968}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.04111293703317642}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5501455068588257}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.6038829684257507}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.6161623597145081}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5910662412643433}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -1.2193617820739746}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.0020070187747478485}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00010859376925509423}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0011855486081913114}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -1.9088062047958374}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -0.36380600929260254}, {"token": "▁to",